{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21451 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside is implicated in the biological activity of SCCH-26 through a series of molecular interactions involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit serves as a target for multiple compounds, including the 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and methyl valerate, which are themselves targets of Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside. The presence of these intermediates suggests a pathway where Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside may modulate the proteasome's function, potentially influencing the activity of SCCH-26. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside could interact with SCCH-26, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence points to a regulatory role of the proteasome in SCCH-26's biological response, but further studies are needed to clarify the precise molecular mechanisms involved.",
